     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":2,\"rationale\":\"The target crown:obtain is an OR step with two parents, h4_0:obtain and h4_1:pivot. Blocking both cuts every route, so 2 blocks are enough. One block is not enough because there are two independent routes. Route 1: edge0 and edge1 give h1_1:escalate (AND), then h2_0:traverse or h3_1:pivot, then h4_0 or h4_1, then crown. Route 2: edge0 or edge1 gives h1_0:obtain or h1_2:escalate, then h3_2:obtain, then h4_0 or h4_1, then crown. Every single candidate leaves a route open. Blocking h1_1, h2_0 or h3_1 leaves route 2. Blocking h1_0, h1_2 or h3_2 leaves route 1. Blocking only h4_0 or only h4_1 leaves the other crown parent reachable. So the minimum is 2.\"}"
    }
   ],
